---
description: Always-on project rules - read the rulebook and the live checkpoint before acting.
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository runs the autonomous kit. Before editing anything:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` - the rulebook that outlives any one milestone.
2. Read `work/CHECKPOINT.md` down to its `## Log` heading - the primary
   objective and the queue.
3. Read `work/AGENT_CONTEXT.md` and `work/DECISIONS.md` - the lessons so far and
   the owner's corrections.
4. Read the canonical task under `work/items/` that the primary objective names.

Read nothing else unless one of those points you there.

Rules the checkers enforce, so following them saves a round trip:

- Instructions, documentation, archives, validators, and hooks are a separate
  lane. Do not edit the paths listed in `autonomous.config.json` under
  `lanes.protectedPaths` while working on a product task.
- Never delete a superseded document; archive it under `docs/archive/` with a
  manifest entry, and give every live document a row in the documentation map.
- Every accepted task gets a plain-language `CHANGELOG.md` entry naming its id.
- Record decisions in `work/messages/`, status in `work/items/`, the current
  outcome in `work/CHECKPOINT.md`, live ownership in the items' `owner` and
  `ownedPaths`, the owner's corrections in `work/DECISIONS.md`. Chat history
  and generated summaries are not authority.

Run `node scripts/work.mjs check` before handing work back. Cursor has no
lifecycle hook, so run `node scripts/context-hook.mjs render` yourself after a
long gap to reload the recorded state.
